\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces  Distribution over explanatory frames (left) and conditional stance distribution within the premodern frame (right). QLoRA substantially increases the probability of premodern framing, while the conditional distribution over stances within that frame remains comparatively stable. The dominant effect of fine-tuning is therefore a redistribution over explanatory regimes rather than a direct modification of stance within regimes. }}{11}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:stacked_bars_labels}{{2}{11}{Distribution over explanatory frames (left) and conditional stance distribution within the premodern frame (right). QLoRA substantially increases the probability of premodern framing, while the conditional distribution over stances within that frame remains comparatively stable. The dominant effect of fine-tuning is therefore a redistribution over explanatory regimes rather than a direct modification of stance within regimes}{figure.2}{}}
